speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, in view of the unprecedented interest of the Canadian public in following the budget presentation and debate and as a matter of importance to this House and to all Canadians, as a matter or urgent and pressing necessity pursuant to Standing Order 43 I move, seconded by the hon. member for Kamloops-Cariboo (Mr. Marchand):
That this House permit Canadian radio and television networks to broadcast the budget presentation by the Minister of Finance (Mr. Turner) and the responses by the first spokesman for each of the opposition parties;
And that the law and the rules and traditions of this House regarding the use of printed reports and the proceedings of the House shall apply to such broadcasts.
